// Title: Use of UltraVNC Remote Access Software
// Sigma ID: 145322e4-0fd3-486b-81ca-9addc75736d8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-10-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: An adversary may use legitimate desktop support and remote access software,to establish an
//   interactive command and control channel to target systems within networks
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/9e5b12c4912c07562aec7500447b11fa3e17e254/atomics/T1219/T1219.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ultravnc.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "VNCViewer" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName =~ "UltraVNC VNCViewer" or ProcessVersionInfoCompanyName =~ "UltraVNC" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "VNCViewer.exe"
